  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: CommAddDisc 6
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: 'A research team creates a short, educational video explaining how scientists
    test new drug compounds in the lab during the discovery stage. They share this
    video with your advocacy organization to get feedback on how to make the explanation
    clearer for patients and families. You suggest different ways that research teams
    can share updates regularly with the community and stress the importance of using
    patient-friendly language.


    In this situation, what impact do community
    advocates have on the research team and community?'
  explanation: "Community advocates help scientists and lab teams share research
    in ways that patients and families can easily understand. By encouraging patient-friendly
    language and regular updates, community advocates help researchers build trust
    with the community. Their feedback ensures that research \u2014 at any stage
    \u2014 is transparent, meaningful, and connected to the needs and perspectives
    of the cancer patient community."
  correctAnswer: 'B: Helping the research team communicate early research information
    effectively and build trust with the community'
  incorrectAnswer1: 'A: Helping the research team recruit patients for clinical trials
    and prevent misconceptions about participation in the community'
  incorrectAnswer2: 'C: Helping the research team decide which drug compounds to
    focus on and produce new treatment options for the community'
  incorrectAnswer3: 'D: None of the above'
  questionRole: Community Advocate
  questionType: MultipleChoice
  questionStage: Discovery
